opentubex (0.38.2) stable; urgency=medium

  [ Highlights ]
  * Profiles can now keep their data, their settings, or both separate. With
    separate data, a profile has its own subscriptions, history, playlists, and
    queue. With separate settings, changes only apply to it, so a car profile
    can hide comments and live chat while sharing your subscriptions.

  [ New features ]
  * Watched comments of yours now also notify you when the video's creator
    hearts them.
  * Typing @ in a comment or reply suggests people from the comments, and
    mentions now link to their channels on YouTube, including the one a reply to
    a reply starts with.
  * Grayscale can now leave downloaded videos in color, while other videos and
    images turn gray.
  * RSS feed episodes and videos from other sites can now be added to the queue.
    The queue also shows while they play and moves on to the next item when one
    ends.
  * RSS feeds now handle podcasts. Find shows in the Apple Podcasts directory,
    import or export your feeds as OPML, and listen to episodes with their title
    and cover. Feeds now show all their items, not only the latest 50.
  * Twitch livestreams now play without Twitch's ads, and also play on iPhone
    and iPad.
  * A new Twitch page in the navigation lists the most watched categories and
    live streams and searches Twitch. Category pages list live streams, videos,
    and clips, which you can filter by language and sort. Twitch searches on the
    Search page can now find categories too.
  * The bottom navigation bar can now show only the current page's label,
    besides showing all labels or none.
  * A new Distraction Free option hides the video title in full window and full
    screen, whether the video plays or is paused. The player menu then opens the
    video information instead.
  * Subscriptions now also show videos that your channels made together with
    another channel that uploaded them. You can turn this off in the
    subscription settings.
  * When you're signed in to YouTube, the comment filters can show only the
    loaded comments and replies written by your channels, along with the
    comments your replies answer.
  * A new UI Density setting makes lists, menus, the side bar, and Settings more
    compact or more spacious. It replaces Compact Settings Categories.
  * Incognito tabs keep the videos you watch and the searches you make out of
    your history and recommendations, and they are never restored or synced.
    Open one from the tab bar or from a video's menu.
  * When you're signed in to YouTube, you can comment on posts and reply to and
    rate their comments, vote in polls and see the results, answer quizzes, and
    like or dislike posts.
  * Right-clicking or long-pressing a channel name or avatar now lets you
    subscribe to or unsubscribe from the channel.
  * A new setting under Appearance lets you click the icon of a tab with a
    playing or paused video to pause or resume it without switching to that tab.
  * You can now pick subscription feeds, such as videos and live streams, that
    refresh together when you refresh one of them.
  * The player menu can now mirror the video, which makes dance, workout, and
    instrument tutorials easier to follow. Turn on Mirror Video under Player
    Controls in the Player Settings to add it.
  * A new Distraction Free setting hides the reason and the feedback buttons
    under each video in Recommended for you on Home.
  * You can hide the refresh errors of a subscribed channel, for example one
    that was terminated but might come back. It still refreshes, and its errors
    can be shown again in its subscription settings.
  * A new Distraction Free setting hides videos you have already watched from
    search results and recommendations, and autoplay skips them.
  * Choose the order of the tabs on the Subscriptions page, for example to put
    the New feed first, in Customize interface.
  * The player menu can now rotate videos that were recorded sideways or upside
    down. Turn on Rotate Video under Player Controls in the Player Settings to
    add it.
  * Playlist downloads can skip videos: uncheck them under Videos in the
    download dialog.
  * Comments can be sorted by Timed, which shows comments about a moment in the
    video as playback reaches it.
  * Press and hold Subscriptions in the navigation to refresh your subscription
    feed in the background without leaving the current page.
  * Signing up for sync now gives you a random 12-word recovery phrase as your
    privacy passphrase and asks you to confirm a few of its words, so your
    encrypted sync data is protected by a passphrase nobody can guess. You can
    still choose your own passphrase with Use custom passphrase instead.
  * You can now pick an app icon from the same palettes as the tray icon. On
    Windows, it also changes pinned taskbar shortcuts and your own Start menu
    and desktop shortcuts.
  * The Download entry in the menus of videos and playlists now lists your
    download templates to start a download right away. Customize… opens the
    download dialog.
  * Video descriptions, channel descriptions, and community posts in other
    languages can now be translated, like comments. The new Translation section
    in General settings turns translations on or off for comments, descriptions,
    and posts separately.

  [ Improvements ]
  * The player's options menu responds faster when you open it, move between its
    views, and close it, especially on slower devices or while the app is busy.
  * The Channels page now also lists the channels you follow on other platforms,
    which moved there from the subscription settings, with a selector that can
    show every platform together. Pasting a channel's address into its search
    field follows the channel.
  * Your YouTube sign-in, sync server credentials, and proxy, Yattee, and
    Invidious passwords are now encrypted with your system's keychain when one
    is available, and Invidious instances get username and password fields. On
    another device or an older version, you enter them again.
  * Live streams with live captions, such as news channels, now also play in up
    to 4K with the built-in engine, and can be rewound with their captions.
  * The app no longer downloads spellchecker dictionaries from Google. Text
    fields no longer underline misspelled words.
  * When Rumble asks you to verify that you're human, for example while you use
    a VPN, you can now do that in the app instead of getting an error.
  * Like in browsers, "Open in a New Tab" now opens the tab in the background,
    so you can queue up several videos without leaving the current page.
  * Opening a video no longer changes your watch history. It joins the history
    once it has played for a few seconds or you seek in it, so checking back on
    the comments leaves your history and saved position as they were.
  * The player's pop-ups for volume, speed, seeking, and zoom have a new look,
    and volume and brightness changes now show a level bar.
  * With the local API, links in video descriptions now show the video title,
    channel handle, or profile name after an icon instead of the full URL.
    Descriptions also list the people mentioned and the podcast a video belongs
    to.
  * Settings has a new look, with colored icons for categories and sections and
    a shorter category list without descriptions.
  * The Stats page has a new design. The summary cards are neutral with an icon
    each, the daily chart is a smooth curve that marks today, and the weekly
    bars are rounded and highlight the current week.
  * The fullscreen side panels now use your theme's colors instead of a fixed
    palette. With a light theme, they stay dark so they remain readable over the
    video. They animate again when you open, close or rearrange them, and resize
    more smoothly.
  * Notifications now open their video, post, or stream in a new tab, so the
    page you were on stays open.
  * The mini player's buttons have a new look, the play button changes shape
    between playing and paused, and all buttons fade out together during
    playback.
  * The Zoom, Volume Boost, and Sleep Timer menus now have a slider like the
    playback speed menu, so you can pick values between the presets, including
    sleep timers of up to two hours.
  * Full Width view no longer stretches each video across the whole window on
    larger screens, and Thumbnail Size now changes how wide the videos get.
  * The notification center now also keeps finished and failed downloads,
    available updates, failed tool updates, blocked syncs, and YouTube sign-outs
    and subscription changes, so they stay around after their pop-up is gone.
  * New upload notifications skip videos that are already in your watch history,
    including ones you watched on another device.
  * Managing automatic downloads now opens right away with many subscriptions,
    and loads more channels as you scroll.
  * Video and channel links you paste into the search bar now appear in your
    search history with the video title or channel name, and typing part of that
    name finds them again.
  * Create a subscription group straight from a channel's subscription settings,
    with that channel already in it.
  * Pinned channels and playlists can be dragged into a new order in the side
    navigation, or by their grips in the More menu on phones. Pinned playlists
    keep that order instead of following the Playlists page.
  * The Local API browser extension for the web app is now a download on each
    release, so you no longer need a copy of the source code to install it.
    Without it, the web app's settings link to its install steps.
  * The New Tab button now sits right after the last tab, like in a browser,
    unless you turn off Show New Tab Button Next to Tabs in Appearance settings.
    The page scrollbar no longer runs behind the header or a bottom tab bar.
  * Notifications in the notification center can now be swiped away on touch
    screens. Ones that no longer apply clear themselves, like a download once
    you play it, and new videos and streams count as read once you watch them.
  * The New feed and the Platforms tab now open in the tabbed view by default.
    You can still switch to the combined view from the subscriptions header.
  * Settings scroll more smoothly, and long lists such as History no longer keep
    the app busy while they wait to load more.
  * The Player Controls settings are now grouped into Audio, Video, Seek Bar and
    Overlay, and Casting, with shorter names, icons, and a one-line description
    for each switch.
  * Scrolling down a video page now pins the player at the top when there's room
    and shows the mini player otherwise. The "Keep player visible when
    scrolling" switch replaces the "When scrolling down" setting.
  * Several settings are simpler: block lists hide, blur, or show matches from
    one menu, Tab Width sizes tabs automatically and Upcoming Videos to Preload
    turns off at their lowest values, and menus choose casting protocols, what
    the system tray does, and what yt-dlp uses your cookies for.
  * Without the grid layout, the player menu shows switches for options that
    turn on or off, instead of On and Off.
  * Switching between Home, Subscriptions, History and Your Playlists is faster,
    especially on phones.
  * Transcripts of long videos open without freezing the page, and side panels
    open and close more smoothly.

  [ Fixed bugs ]
  * Seeking back in a live stream now plays from the chosen moment instead of
    seconds or even minutes after it.
  * Live streams that can't be rewound far no longer keep stalling with a
    countdown over the video, or reload after a few minutes, also after
    returning to live.
  * The player controls no longer fade away while the pointer rests on the seek
    bar, a button, or the fullscreen title and actions.
  * Downloaded videos now play from the download when you open them from a link
    or a tab synced from another device, instead of streaming them.
  * Automatic sync pauses less often after you delete items on one of your
    devices, and Sync settings now shows when it is paused and how to resume it.
  * Twitch clips now start at your default quality when they offer it, instead
    of the lowest one.
  * Replies to replies now appear under the reply they answer instead of in one
    list at the end of the thread. Your replies nest there on YouTube too.
  * When replies fail to load from YouTube and Invidious fallback is on, they
    now load from Invidious instead of adding the comments again.
  * Going back to a long list, such as your watch history, now returns to the
    videos you were looking at instead of further down.
  * Playlist downloads follow the Concurrent Downloads setting and download
    several videos at once, each with its own progress bar, instead of one after
    another.
  * 360° and VR videos play in VR mode again instead of failing with a player
    error, and VR180 videos show their half sphere instead of a stretched flat
    view that wraps around.
  * Downloading a live stream now shows how much has been recorded, and Stop
    recording saves the recording instead of losing it.
  * Fixed a crash that closed the command palette and left the interface
    unresponsive when searching items whose titles contain emojis.
  * When queued videos play in the middle of a playlist, the playlist now
    continues with its next video once the queue is done, instead of being left
    behind.
  * Videos no longer restart or switch to legacy formats in a loop when their
    captions fail to load.
  * Videos show a loading spinner until they start playing, instead of a play
    button that made them look paused.
  * Videos you open from notifications, links, or anywhere else now leave the
    New feed, not only videos opened from the feed itself.
  * Casting works with more receivers: Google Cast no longer stops right after a
    video starts loading on Google TV, YouTube live streams play over Google
    Cast, the FCast desktop receiver plays YouTube videos, and DLNA renderers
    resume where you left off.
  * Auto-translated captions load again without a signed-in account, instead of
    failing because YouTube refuses the request.
  * Playlists synced with your YouTube account now show their videos in the same
    order as on YouTube, including videos you moved there.
  * Turning autoplay on or off from the player no longer pauses or resumes the
    video.

 -- OpenTubeX contributors <info@opentubex.org>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:11:20 +0000
